pssssst Three horses, ten laps. Run it again for a different winner.
pssssst
pssssst Each lap, each horse adds its stride (one) to its distance. But:
pssssst   a horse that sulks or runs away stops moving, and nobody cures it;
pssssst   a horse that starts lying claims a stride of two, and gets away with it;
pssssst   a horse that falls out with its own distance refuses to add to it;
pssssst   and if the lap counter itself gets in a mood, the race is abandoned.

